   443→
   444→\section{Error Analysis}
   445→\label{sec:theory}
   446→
   447→We derive local and global error bounds for the adaptive FSP method based on probability fluxes across the truncation boundary. Let $\mathcal{X}$ denote the full state space and $J \subset \mathcal{X}$ be a finite active set. Define the complement $J' := \mathcal{X} \setminus J$ with $J \cap J' = \emptyset$ and $J \cup J' = \mathcal{X}$. The generator matrix admits a natural block decomposition:
   448→
   449→\begin{equation}
   450→\label{eq:block-partition}
   451→\mathbf{A}=
   452→\begin{pmatrix}
   453→\mathbf{A}_{JJ} & \mathbf{A}_{JJ'}\\
   454→\mathbf{A}_{J'J} & \mathbf{A}_{J'J'}
   455→\end{pmatrix}, 
   456→\qquad
   457→\boldsymbol{p}(t)=
   458→\begin{pmatrix}
   459→\boldsymbol{p}_J(t)\\
   460→\boldsymbol{p}_{J'}(t)
   461→\end{pmatrix},
   462→\end{equation}
   463→Recall that under the column convention $\mathbf{A}_{ij} > 0$ represents a transition rate \emph{from} state $j$ \emph{to} state $i$. Accordingly, the block subscripts follow matrix index order (rows, columns): $\mathbf{A}_{JJ} \in \mathbb{R}^{|J| \times |J|}$ has rows and columns in $J$ and governs transitions within $J$; $\mathbf{A}_{J'J} \in \mathbb{R}^{|J'| \times |J|}$ has rows in $J'$ and columns in $J$, so its entries $(\mathbf{A}_{J'J})_{\boldsymbol{y}\boldsymbol{x}} = \mathbf{A}_{\boldsymbol{y}\boldsymbol{x}}$ for $\boldsymbol{y} \in J'$, $\boldsymbol{x} \in J$ describe transitions \emph{from} $J$ \emph{to} $J'$ (outflux); symmetrically, $\mathbf{A}_{JJ'} \in \mathbb{R}^{|J| \times |J'|}$ describes transitions \emph{from} $J'$ \emph{to} $J$ (influx). See Figure~\ref{fig:transitions}. The partitioned CME becomes:
   464→\begin{equation}
   465→\label{eq:partitioned-cme}
   466→\frac{d}{dt}
   467→\begin{pmatrix}
   468→\boldsymbol{p}_J(t) \\
   469→\boldsymbol{p}_{J'}(t)
   470→\end{pmatrix}
   471→=
   472→\begin{pmatrix}
   473→\mathbf{A}_{JJ} & \mathbf{A}_{JJ'}\\
   474→\mathbf{A}_{J'J} & \mathbf{A}_{J'J'}
   475→\end{pmatrix}
   476→\begin{pmatrix}
   477→\boldsymbol{p}_J(t) \\
   478→\boldsymbol{p}_{J'}(t)
   479→\end{pmatrix},
   480→\end{equation}
   481→where, 
   482→\begin{equation}
   483→\label{eq:row-sum-identities}
   484→\mathbf{1}^\top \mathbf{A}_{JJ} = -\mathbf{1}^\top \mathbf{A}_{J'J}, \qquad \mathbf{1}^\top \mathbf{A}_{J'J'} = -\mathbf{1}^\top \mathbf{A}_{JJ'}.
   485→\end{equation}
   486→The column sum property of the generator $\mathbf{A}$ immediately yields the identities in Eq.~\eqref{eq:row-sum-identities}.
   487→\begin{figure}[ht!]
   488→    \centering
   489→    \begin{tikzpicture}[node distance=3cm, auto, thick]
   490→    \tikzstyle{state} = [circle, draw, minimum size=1cm, text centered]
   491→    \tikzstyle{transition} = [->, thick]
   492→    \node[state] (S) at (0, 0) {$J$};
   493→    \node[state] (R) at (4, 0) {$J'$};
   494→    \path[transition, loop left] (S) edge node[left] {$\mathbf{A}_{JJ}$} (S);
   495→    \path[transition, loop right] (R) edge node[right] {$\mathbf{A}_{J'J'}$} (R);
   496→    \path[transition] (S) edge[bend left=20] node[above] {$\mathbf{A}_{J'J}$} (R);
   497→    \path[transition] (R) edge[bend left=20] node[below] {$\mathbf{A}_{JJ'}$} (S);
   498→    \end{tikzpicture}

