  1119→\subsection{Performance Evaluation of Matrix Construction}
  1120→
  1121→In this subsection we evaluate the matrix construction strategy introduced in Section~\ref{sec:matrix_construction}. The forward enumeration approach constructs the generator by iterating through reactions for each state, directly computing destination states as $y = x + \nu_k$. We benchmark this strategy against a standard implementation that uses backward state expansion on the Oregonator, ROBER, and toggle switch models.
